.env

*.test
coverage.out

# Agent worktrees. They are git worktrees of this repository, so `git add -A` sees them as
# embedded repositories and commits a gitlink pointing at a path that exists on one
# machine. It happened once, in the same commit that fixed two other people's oversights.
/.claude/
